.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EVP_MAC-SIPHASH 7ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_MAC-Siphash
.Nd The Siphash EVP_MAC implementation
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Support for computing Siphash MACs through the
.Sy EVP_MAC
API.
.Ss Identity
This implementation is identified with this name and properties, to be
used with
.Xr EVP_MAC_fetch 3 :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqSIPHASH", \(dqprovider=default"
.El
.Ss Supported parameters
The general description of these parameters can be found in
.Xr EVP_MAC 3 .
.Pp
All these parameters can be set with
.Xr EVP_MAC_CTX_set_params 3 .
Furthermore, the "size" parameter can be retrieved with
.Xr EVP_MAC_CTX_get_params 3 ,
or with
.Xr EVP_MAC_CTX_get_mac_size 3 .
The length of the "size" parameter should not exceed that of a
.Sy size_t .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqkey" ( Ns Sy OSSL_MAC_PARAM_KEY Ns ) <octet string>
Sets the MAC key.
Setting this parameter is identical to passing a
.Em key
to
.Xr EVP_MAC_init 3 .
.It \(dqsize" ( Ns Sy OSSL_MAC_PARAM_SIZE Ns ) <unsigned integer>
Sets the MAC size.
.It \(dqc-rounds" ( Ns Sy OSSL_MAC_PARAM_C_ROUNDS Ns ) <unsigned integer>
Specifies the number of rounds per message block.
By default this is
.Em 2 .
.It \(dqd-rounds" ( Ns Sy OSSL_MAC_PARAM_D_ROUNDS Ns ) <unsigned integer>
Specifies the number of finalisation rounds.
By default this is
.Em 4 .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr EVP_MAC_CTX_get_params 3 ,
.Xr EVP_MAC_CTX_set_params 3 ,
.Xr EVP_MAC 3 ,
.Xr OSSL_PARAM 3
